# Keezly — SwiftFormat configuration.
#
# Deliberately an *allowlist*. SwiftFormat's full rule set disagrees with the
# hand-set style in this repository in ways that would cost readability rather
# than gain it — `consecutiveSpaces` flattens the aligned trailing comments that
# explain the rules, `hoistPatternLet` hides which bindings a case introduces,
# and `wrapPropertyBodies` expands one-line computed properties for no benefit.
#
# So the formatter runs only the rules nobody argues about: whitespace hygiene
# and import order. Style beyond that is enforced by review and by SwiftLint,
# which catches things that actually cause bugs.
#
# Recorded as DEC-016.

--swiftversion 6.0
--exclude .build,Packages/KeezlyCore/.build,vendor,Keezly.xcodeproj

--rules sortImports,duplicateImports,trailingSpace,consecutiveBlankLines,linebreakAtEndOfFile,emptyBraces,spaceInsideParens,spaceInsideBrackets,blankLinesAtEndOfScope,redundantParens

--emptybraces no-space
